# AlgoQuest MVP

AlgoQuest turns DSA practice into tactical, visual coding quests. This repository is a production-minded MVP: a Next.js player experience, an Express API, a sandbox-executor contract, PostgreSQL schema, Docker deployment configuration, and an implementation guide.

## Quick start

1. Install Node.js 20+, Docker, and pnpm 11.16+ (`corepack enable` then `corepack prepare pnpm@11.16.0 --activate`).
2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set the values.
3. Install dependencies with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
4. Start the web, API, and data dependencies with `docker compose up --build`.
5. Open `http://localhost:3000` and `http://localhost:4000/health`.

For the full architecture, data model, security model, API contract, curriculum, deployment plan, and 30-day roadmap, read [the implementation guide](docs/implementation-guide.md).

The execution service deliberately has no Docker socket in Compose. To enable actual submissions in a hardened runner environment, pre-build the pinned sandbox images (`algoquest-python:1` and `algoquest-cpp:1`) from `services/executor/images/`, then configure the executor with your isolated worker platform. This preserves the critical separation between public services and untrusted code execution.

## GitHub and deployment

The repository is ready for GitHub: pull requests and `main` pushes run type checks, a Next.js production build, and Docker image builds. Version tags such as `v0.1.0` publish `web`, `api`, and `executor` images to GitHub Container Registry (GHCR).

1. Create an empty GitHub repository, then add this folder and push the `main` branch.
2. In the repository's **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables**, create `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` with the public HTTPS address of the deployed API, for example `https://api.example.com`.
3. Protect `main` and require the `CI / verify` and `CI / docker-build` checks before merging.
4. Push a semantic version tag to publish images: `git tag v0.1.0 && git push origin v0.1.0`.
5. Deploy `ghcr.io/<your-owner>/algoquest-web:<version>` and `ghcr.io/<your-owner>/algoquest-api:<version>` to your container host; use managed PostgreSQL/Redis and keep the executor private.

See [the GitHub deployment guide](docs/github-deployment.md) for environment variables and rollout details. GitHub Pages is not suitable for the full app because it cannot run the API, database, or secure executor.

## Repository layout

```
apps/web/             Next.js player experience
services/api/         Express REST API and submission orchestration
services/executor/    Isolated runner service (Docker-based design + starter)
packages/contracts/   Shared API domain types
infra/postgres/       PostgreSQL schema and seed data
docs/                 Product and technical design
```

## MVP boundaries

The API has a usable development evaluator so the UI flow works without Docker. Production submissions must set `EXECUTOR_URL` and use the dedicated executor service; never execute untrusted code in the API process.

